\\")]; assert len(methods) >= 2'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The public tests exercise the requested newline normalization behavior, including CRLF, lone CR, existing LF, other characters, and trailing newlines.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read test_solution.py and determine whether its unittest test methods exercise the public API for CRLF and lone CR replacement with LF, preservation of existing LF and other characters, and preservation of the number of line breaks including trailing newlines. Pass only if these cases are covered by tests that invoke the public API.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The refactor preserves both public signatures, return types, error behavior, input immutability, imports, public names, and type hints while having both functions delegate the shared algorithm to one private helper.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read solution.py and test_solution.py. Assess whether normalize and normalize_legacy preserve their pre-refactor signatures, return types, error behavior, input immutability, import compatibility, public names, and type hints, and delegate the shared algorithm to exactly one private helper. Compare signatures and error behavior with any existing implementation or tests available in the workspace; if no evidence establishes a detail, do not assume it is preserved.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named files are relative to the supplied task workspace; solution.py and test_solution.py may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"The existing public signatures, return types, error behavior, import compatibility, public names, and type hints can be determined from the supplied workspace before editing.\\\",\\\"The unittest discovery command is the requested verification command; its suite is discoverable with `python -m unittest discover -v`.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":21169,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":730,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
